      children: [(0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(_components.strong, {
        children: "Osho Darshan:"
      }), " The definition is stunning in its simplicity: the body is a field because in it the harvest of a lifetime is reaped — pleasure, pain, memory, karma ripening like crops. And the one who ", (0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(_components.em, {
        children: "knows"
      }), " the field is the knower. Osho underlines the implication: the body is known, therefore the body is not the knower. You say \"my body\" — who says that? The one who says \"my body\" cannot be the body. This is the first rung of the whole chapter's ladder: before any philosophy, simply notice the owner of the word \"my.\" That owner is the knower, and it is closer than your skin."]
