      children: [(0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(_components.strong, {
        children: "Osho Darshan:"
      }), " The chapter ends where it began, with the eye of knowledge — the seeing that distinguishes field from knower, and sees the liberation of beings from Nature. Osho reads the final words as a quiet triumph: \"they go to the Supreme\" — not they will, but they do; the journey and the destination are the same seeing. When the distinction is perceived, Nature's grip is loosened and the many knowers are known as one. This is the whole Gita's Jnana Yoga in one verse: see the field as field, the knower as knower, and the union of the two as the one light. That seeing is not the beginning of the path; it is the path's end, walking."]
